      "id": "word-al--method",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "al",
      "answerEn": "with; by means of the (a + el, introducing a method)",
      "noteEn": "Al is the required contraction of a and el. In some technical expressions, it introduces the tool or process used, as in al láser and al arco.",
      "example": {
        "es": "La pieza se cortó al láser.",
        "en": "The piece was laser-cut."
      },
      "tags": ["word", "method", "contraction", "technical", "B1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-arco--electric-arc",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "arco",
      "answerEn": "electric arc",
      "noteEn": "In welding, arco is the bright electrical discharge that supplies intense heat. This is different from arco meaning a bow or a curved arch.",
      "example": {
        "es": "El arco eléctrico produce mucho calor.",
        "en": "The electric arc produces a great deal of heat."
      },
      "tags": ["word", "electricity", "welding", "technical", "B1"]
    },
    {
      "id": "word-rabito--cherry-stem",
      "kind": "word",
      "promptEs": "rabito",
      "answerEn": "little stem; cherry stem",
      "noteEn": "Rabito adds the ending -ito to rabo. That ending often makes something sound small; with fruit, rabito can name the short stalk or stem.",
      "example": {
        "es": "Quitó el rabito de la fresa.",
        "en": "She removed the strawberry's little stem."
      },
      "tags": ["word", "fruit", "diminutive", "B1"]
